    "uid": "29da5ef8168f11668cb4f1a9324bc7a3",
    "title": "Root CA certificate installed",
    "desc": "A program dropped a certificate into the system trust store (ca-trust anchors, ca-certificates) or ran the tool that rebuilds it (update-ca-trust, update-ca-certificates, certctl, trust). A new root CA in the system store makes the host trust any certificate the attacker signs, which is how TLS interception and traffic subversion are set up (MITRE T1553.004). Installing a trusted root is a rare, high-privilege act outside of provisioning, so on a running host it is a clean alarm.",
